  "Bug_Details": "Use Random.nextInt(int).  Random.nextInt() % n can have negative results Random.nextInt() % n has a 1/n chance of being 0\na 1/2n chance of being each number from 1 to n-1 inclusive\na 1/2n chance of being each number from -1 to -(n-1) inclusive Many users expect a uniformly distributed random integer between 0 and n-1\ninclusive, but you must use random.nextInt(n) to get that behavior. If the\noriginal behavior is truly desired, use (random.nextBoolean() ? 1 : -1) *\nrandom.nextInt(n).",
